# Allow always: option 2 on the first prompt, then the same command again. The
# scenario ends on whatever the second call shows (a prompt or the result).
name: tool-always
size: 100x30
args: --permission-mode default
prompt: Create the marker file
files: ../../../testdata/fixtures/12/app
script: scripts/tool-always.json
parity: PD-08, PD-02
---
ready
wait_for 30s Do you want to proceed?
settle
keys 2
wait_for 30s Created parity-marker.txt.
settle
checkpoint allowed-always
type Do it again
keys enter
wait_for 30s touch parity-marker.txt again
settle 5s
checkpoint second-call
